<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlos Saavedra Lamas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1959</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlos Saavedra Lamas was an Argentine jurist and foreign minister from 1932 to 1938. He drafted an anti-war treaty signed by many American states in 1933 and helped mediate the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaco-war">Chaco War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>, for which he received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1936, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American to win a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlos-saavedra-lamas.jpg" alt="Carlos Saavedra Lamas" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carlos_Saavedra_Lamas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
